{
    "$comment": [
        "Which learn.forwardedu.com content appears on the editor home page, and in what order (Brian, 2026-10-08).",
        "One category is one row of cards. An item is either a post share link (post id + MakeCode share id; converted into a self-contained tutorial under docs/forward/projects/) or a tutorial already in a Forward extension, served from the snapshot at its pinned tag.",
        "tutorial items: \"tag\" is the release the markdown is taken from (the latest, which carries the fixes); the card opens it at the version its own package block pins, so the project depends on a single version of the extension.",
        "hidden: kept in the snapshot but left off the home page, with the reason. forward/content/learn/inventory.csv lists everything on the site and why the rest is out.",
        "Edit this file, then run: node forward/build/learn-fetch.js (network) and node forward/build/learn-gallery.js (offline).",
        "extensions: what a converted share project depends on. Each share link is re-pinned to the current release of its extension (keyed by owner/repo, lower case), so it opens on makecode.microbit.org too and downloads with a pre-built native image (forward/native-combos.json). \"replace\" moves a retired extension to its successor; \"drop\" removes a dependency the successor already brings in.",
        "tutorialRepins: extension tutorials whose package block pins a release that pulls pxt-jacdac 1.9.38 or 1.9.40, which has no pre-built native image, so Download would fail. Our served copy pins the given release instead (pxt-jacdac 1.9.41). Each tutorial's final program was compiled under both pins with identical results (2026-10-08). pxt-robot-tour is not listed: even its latest release (v1.0.4) uses pxt-jacdac 1.9.38.",
        "image (per category): picture for cards whose content has none, from the site's media library."
    ],
    "extensions": {
        "forward-education/pxt-all-fwd-blocks": {
            "name": "all-fwd-blocks",
